```cpp
hb_vector_t<char> buf;
unsigned int buf_size = _plan_estimate_subset_table_size (plan, source_blob->length);
...
if (unlikely (!buf.alloc (buf_size)))
```

`buf.alloc(buf_size)` only allocates memory but does NOT initialize it! It calls `realloc()` under the hood, which doesn't zero the memory. The buffer is NOT zeroed.

Then:
```cpp
hb_serialize_context_t serializer ((void *) buf, buf_size);
```

The serializer uses this uninitialized buffer. Now let me check the serializer constructor:

